# Every consumer of this repository is Linux: the container images, the CI
# runners, and the server. Nothing here is read by a Windows program, so the
# working copy is normalised to LF too — a carriage return can only arrive as
# a defect, and it arrives silently.
#
# Two ways this has actually bitten:
#   * a heredoc terminator carrying a carriage return never matches, which
#     reads like a syntax error in your own script;
#   * `git archive` applies core.autocrlf, so on Windows the archive of a
#     commit is not the commit — the Caddyfile and the compose files reached
#     the server with CRLF on the first deploy.
* text=auto eol=lf
